  "2026-07-27T13:20:31.866Z","harness:codex","Scope decision: command tiering remains related to this SDK context-contract bundle, but the current implementation will not claim full help/MCP/completion/docs derivation; returning it to open until that acceptance surface is actively edited."
  "2026-07-27T16:42:27.992Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: active in the shared runtime-capability-contracts bundle. Duplicate check covered all 2,136 tracker items and live GitHub reports; this item owns a distinct acceptance facet and will share exact-head verification with the related active items."
  "2026-07-27T18:19:12.348Z","harness:codex","Foundation evidence: every built-in and extension command has a validated tier contract; MCP profiles, generated docs, and completion command sets consume it. Remaining acceptance before closure: route CLI help visibility through the tier field, add the explicit one-screen core-help budget assertion, and prove a single tier edit changes all four rendered surfaces in one snapshot. Returning to open/released rather than overstating completion."
  "2026-07-30T06:47:40.277Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: command enumeration retains aliases and now emits canonical_command plus core/compatibility/extended visibility in both detailed and summary projections."
  "2026-07-30T07:18:57.436Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary: this PR exposes canonical visibility on command-scoped/full contracts and preserves the existing shared tier registry, MCP, completion, and generated-doc gates. CLI help routing and the one-field four-surface snapshot/budget proof remain; returning open without claiming the complete single-source migration."
  "2026-07-30T07:26:28.388Z","harness:codex","Token-efficiency evidence: command visibility and canonical identity remain available in command-scoped contracts, while unscoped/full projections omit repeated semantic rows. This preserves the visibility primitive without increasing the all-in-one context surface beyond its enforced budget."
